      "result": "## Summary\n\nI have completed comprehensive testing of the resume-building webapp against all 21 checklist items. Here are the results:\n\n**PASSED (16 items):**\n- FT-1 through FT-8: Core resume creation, editing, template selection, preview, duplication, and search/sort functionality all working correctly\n- CS-10: Consistent date format and current position handling working properly\n- IX-12 through IX-14: Immediate preview updates and session-based content retention working\n- CT-15 through CT-18, CT-20: Content rendering and preservation across navigation working correctly\n\n**FAILED (5 items):**\n1. **FT-19**: Date filtering not implemented - no UI controls for filtering by creation date or date range\n2. **CS-9**: Date validation not enforced - accepted end dates before start dates and future dates without errors\n3. **CS-11**: New resume persistence issue - resumes created in session are lost after page reload (only pre-seeded resumes persist)\n4. **CS-21**: Empty title validation not enforced - accepted empty strings as resume titles without rejection\n\n**Key Strengths:**\n- Smooth resume creation and multi-template support with instant preview updates\n- Effective content management (add, edit, delete, reorder sections and entries)\n- Good search and sort capabilities (title search is case-insensitive)\n- Proper duplicate resume independence\n\n**Key Issues:**\n- Missing date filtering feature entirely\n- No date range validation for work/education entries\n- Poor persistence layer (new user-created resumes don't survive reload)\n- Insufficient form validation (empty titles allowed)\n\nThe application provides solid core functionality for resume building but needs work on data validation, persistence, and the date filtering feature.",
